# Binary files must NEVER go through line-ending conversion.
#
# Why this file exists: on the first `git add`, Git classified
# fixtures/...(synthetic).pdf as TEXT and warned that "LF will be replaced by
# CRLF the next time Git touches it". A reportlab-generated PDF has no early NUL
# bytes, so Git's text/binary heuristic guesses wrong — and rewriting bytes in a
# PDF or xlsx corrupts it. That would silently invalidate the validation corpus
# on clone, which is precisely what tracking these files is meant to prevent.
#
# The vendor documents behind the 20/20 hand-verified accuracy result are only
# meaningful if they are byte-identical to what was tested.

*.pdf   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.xlsm  binary
*.xls   binary
*.docx  binary
*.doc   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.zip   binary
*.p12   binary
*.pfx   binary

# SVG is genuinely text (XML) — diffable, safe to normalize.
*.svg   text

# Keep certificates/keys byte-exact if one is ever tracked deliberately.
*.pem   -text
*.cer   -text
*.crt   -text
